                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "You don't have to go through the trouble of turning off monitoring. You can if you want to, but I think it is only going to save a few milliseconds on startup.\n\nIt might be simpler to have a std::set<std::string> that contains the property names to display. Or a std::map<std::string,bool> with the property names and whether they should be printed. That would eliminate the hardcoded vector offsets in the code here and below."
                },
